.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-sales-buyers - List deduplicated buyers for a product


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad sales buyers [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the unique buyers who purchased one or more products.

.PP
Buyers are deduplicated by email and aggregated across every page, so a buyer
who purchased more than once appears a single time with a purchase count and
their most recent purchase date. UTM fields in JSON, CSV, and plain output come
from the buyer's most recent attributed purchase, and stay empty when no
purchase came through a UTM link. If attributed purchases have the same
timestamp, the first sale returned by the API wins. Use gumroad sales export for
the full per-sale web CSV by email.

.PP
Pass --product more than once to union buyers across a relaunched listing's old
and new IDs and dedupe them in one shot.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--after\fP=""
	Filter sales after date (YYYY-MM-DD)

.PP
\fB--before\fP=""
	Filter sales before date (YYYY-MM-DD)

.PP
\fB--csv\fP[=false]
	Output as CSV

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for buyers

.PP
\fB--product\fP=[]
	Filter by product ID (repeatable)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad sales buyers --product <id>
  gumroad sales buyers --product <old-id> --product <new-id>
  gumroad sales buyers --product <id> --after 2024-01-01 --csv
  gumroad sales buyers --product <id> --json --jq '.buyers[].email'
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-sales(1)\fP
